@*
    An archive box: a lid across the top, the box under it, and a handle slot
    on its face.

    Drawn here rather than fetched, for the reason ChevronUpIcon gives, and in
    Lucide's idiom on exactly the terms `.devbook/design/typography-and-layout.md#iconography`
    allows: an outline on the 24x24 grid, stroked at 2, round caps and joins,
    filled nowhere. Lucide's `archive`.

    Named for the shape, not for a meaning. The shell header puts it on the Show
    archived toggle; the name the toggle answers to stays on the toggle, so the
    glyph is decorative and hidden from assistive technology.
*@

<svg class="@ClassValue"
     viewBox="0 0 24 24"
     width="@Size"
     height="@Size"
     fill="none"
     stroke="currentColor"
     stroke-width="2"
     stroke-linecap="round"
     stroke-linejoin="round"
     aria-hidden="true"
     focusable="false"
     data-testid="@TestId"
     @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
    @* The lid, the box under it, then the handle slot. The lid is Lucide's rect
       written as a path, so the glyph is paths only like the rest of the set. *@
    <path d="M3 3h18a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H3a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1z" />
    <path d="M4 8v11a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8" />
    <path d="M10 12h4" />
</svg>

@code {
    /// <summary>Edge length, written straight onto <c>width</c> and <c>height</c>;
    /// see <see cref="ChevronUpIcon.Size"/> for the scale it is drawn on.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Size { get; set; } = "16";

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    private string ClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? "archive-icon" : $"archive-icon {CssClass}";
}
